Low-power wait proof:
1. profile 2 enabled PL011 receive and receive-timeout wake events through the
   QEMU virt GICv2 distributor and CPU interface
2. host.read cleared stale wake state, rechecked the receive FIFO, and executed
   WFI only while it remained empty
3. after the compile-rejection ready marker, QEMU remained at 0.0 percent CPU
   for four one-second samples with no serial input
4. a valid request delivered after that delay woke the same machine, which ran
   the child and exited with status zero after the zero terminator
5. no Gaut QEMU process remained after the delayed-input run

