Machine:
- QEMU 11.1.0, virt board, Cortex-A53, 128 MiB RAM
- no network device
- compiler loaded directly with -kernel dist/gaut-os.img

Boundary:
- the guest contains no Linux, libc, dynamic loader, Python, C, Rust, LLVM,
  assembler, linker, or foreign runtime
- the host shell only frames and streams exact requests and QEMU emulates the
  machine
- compiler and child ordinary Gaut memory are separated, but there is no MMU
  or malicious-child fault containment
- the retained launcher supplies a bounded serial stream, while the resident
  host.read path can wait for delayed input without consuming a host CPU core
- complete invalid Gaut source requests recover to ready, but malformed lengths
  and child hardware faults do not yet recover
- the next verified gate is splitting the compiler across Module v0 units,
  followed by named in-memory source storage in docs/ROADMAP.md
